# cifarium: headers for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages. Both read a file named `_headers` in the
# folder you publish, in this format. Copy this file there and keep its name. If the build
# folder is a subfolder of your site, put its path in front of every path below
# (/cifarium/index.html, /cifarium/vendor/*, ...).
#
# The model computes in several threads only on a page that is cross-origin isolated. The two
# headers make it so. They go on the page that runs the model, on cifarium-worker.js and on
# vendor/: ONNX Runtime starts its own threads from the files there, and an isolated page
# refuses a thread script that does not carry them, so the model would not start at all.
# If your own page runs the model instead of index.html, add the same two headers to it.
#
# `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` blocks images, scripts and fonts from other sites
# that do not allow it. Put the headers only on the pages that run the model.
#
# vendor/ and models/ have the version in their paths, so their files never change at an
# address and may be kept for a year. Nothing else here may be: cifarium.json, cifarium.js,
# cifarium-worker.js, index.html and data/ change at the same address when you build again.
#
# A Content-Security-Policy is your site's and is not set here. The model needs no 'unsafe-eval'
# and no 'unsafe-inline'; a strict policy on every file of the folder works:
#   Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'
# With `host: hub` the worker downloads the model from Hugging Face and its CDN, so add
#   connect-src 'self' https://huggingface.co https://*.hf.co
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' is needed where WebAssembly is compiled: on cifarium-worker.js and vendor/
# if the policy reaches them. index.html has its script inline, which `script-src 'self'` stops:
# under such a policy run the model from a script file of your own page. Trusted Types
# (`require-trusted-types-for`) stop the worker from starting. Over plain http on a host other
# than localhost the page is not a secure context: the two headers below are ignored, so the
# model computes in one thread, and without the browser store (Cache API) the runtime keeps
# nothing between visits. Serve the site over https.

/
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/index.html
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/cifarium-worker.js
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/vendor/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
